	abstract = {In the context of the new power system, it is particularly important to strengthen and optimize the grid planning and investment management process, in which the accurate prediction of the cost level of substation projects has become a key link in the investment decision of power grid enterprises. To this end, an intelligent grid substation project cost prediction algorithm based on Random Forest and Pelican Optimization Algorithm (POA) to improve Support Vector Machines (SVM) is proposed. Firstly, grid substation project cost features are screened based on the random forest algorithm to eliminate redundant variables. Secondly, SVM is selected as the basic method of the prediction model, and POA optimizes the SVM model parameters to improve the generalization ability and prediction accuracy of the model. Finally, the grid project cost prediction model of RF-POA-SVM is constructed, which provides in-depth analyses and predictions of the grid project cost data collected in Shanghai for the years 2021-2023. The experimental results show that the RF-POA-SVM intelligent prediction model proposed in this paper can achieve the prediction of grid project cost more accurately, and combined with a variety of factors such as economic, social and technological development, it puts forward the proposal of optimization measures for the level of Shanghai grid project cost, which will have theoretical and practical significance for the future prediction of grid project cost.  © 2025 IEEE.},
