	abstract = {With the rapid integration of Renewable Energy Sources (RESs) for power generation introduces greater uncertainties. The real time optimal power flow (OPF) solution is required faster and with greater accuracy. This paper develops and compare a machine learning and a deep learning approach for optimizing the real-time operation of electric power grids. In particular, feasible solutions to the OPF problem are realized with no violations in constraints and negligible optimality gaps. The aim of the OPF problem is identifying optimal operational conditions that minimize the power losses and/or generation costs or any other objective function that we aim for. Due to the computational challenges which occur while solving this nonconvex problem, many efforts have been made on linearizing or approximating the problem in order to solve the OPF on faster timescales. However, even after many approximations of the actual system state, there is still a need to solve an optimization problem, which can be time consuming for large networks. In this work, an approach to remove one of the OPF constraint entirely prior to building models using machine learning and deep learning, enabling us to Find nearly optimal and realizable OPF solutions. This allows us to skip the nonconvexity of OPF problem, resulting in a significant decrease in computational burden.  © 2023 IEEE.},
